   "note": "Cliopatria's Pallava shape moves north-east in 451 to cover the Nellore coast and the Krishna–Penner country, so only Tondaimandalam round Kanchipuram is added here, between that shape, the Western Gangas (Kolar) and the Kalabhra polygon. The reign of Vishnugopavarman II (c. 500–525) is described as a time of upheaval from the Kalabhra invasion of the Tamil country, but no source says Kanchi itself was lost; the Pallava kings of these decades continue to issue grants as kings of Kanchi. Reign dates follow the Sastri chronology quoted on Wikipedia and are approximate. Drawn from a hand-traced extent, then cut back wherever the atlas already draws another state in the same years (Cliopatria realms and the other reconstruction layers), so it joins Cliopatria's own Pallava shape without overlapping it.",
