   "note": "Nandivarman III, allied with the Western Gangas, the Rashtrakutas and the Cholas, defeated the Pandya Srimara at Tellaru (near Vandavasi; Wikipedia dates it 830, which does not fit Nandivarman's reign as dated here, so the year is uncertain) and pursued the Pandyas to the Vaigai; Srimara recovered and defeated the allies at Kudamukku (Kumbakonam), c. 859. The region is drawn as Tondaimandalam with Naduvil Nadu (the country between the Ponnaiyar and the Vellar), the area the Pallavas held between the Pandya advance and Nripatunga's recovery; the southern edge on the Vellar is a reconstruction. Nandivarman divided the kingdom before his death between Nripatunga (south) and Kampavarman (north). The north is under Cliopatria's Rashtrakuta polygon and is not drawn. Drawn from a hand-traced extent, then cut back wherever the atlas already draws another state in the same years (Cliopatria realms and the other reconstruction layers), so it joins Cliopatria's own Pallava shape without overlapping it.",
