   "note": "Nripatunga defeated Srimara on the Arisil river and recovered the southern lands lost under Dantivarman; his Bahour (Puducherry) copper plates of his 8th regnal year record grants there. After the battle of Sripurambiyam near Kumbakonam (c. 879–885), where Aparajita, the Western Gangas and the Cholas defeated the Pandya Varaguna II, the Cholas gained territory round Thanjavur (Cliopatria draws the Chola state there; its larger shape from 886 trims this region at the Kollidam). The region is drawn to the Kollidam (Coleroon), the northern edge of the Chola country. Pallava rule ended when Aditya I Chola defeated and killed Aparajita and annexed Tondaimandalam, c. 897 (Wikipedia; Sastri gives c. 890 for the battle and Schwartzberg's plate notes 890 and 893); from 898 Cliopatria's Chola Empire covers Tondaimandalam. The north is under Cliopatria's Rashtrakuta polygon and is not drawn. Drawn from a hand-traced extent, then cut back wherever the atlas already draws another state in the same years (Cliopatria realms and the other reconstruction layers), so it joins Cliopatria's own Pallava shape without overlapping it.",
